From 349318a0600917bad8f391ad628fa0c7f134b3f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:55:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Keep every browser chain consumer on the confirmed
 profile's routes

Independent mode (confirmed profile):
- balances, the page's gas estimate and the payer code check read only the
  profile's RPCs (wallet.js, fund.js, pay.js); the wallet is asked only to sign
  and broadcast; no read falls back to the wallet's provider
- custody reads use every profile RPC with its quorum, confirmations and
  block-age limit (custody.js), not the first three with a fixed 2
- grant page session reads use the profile quorum client, not rpcs[0]
- all routes down: transactions refuse by name ('none of the network
  profile's RPC endpoints...'), receipts report the outage; an invalid or
  unconfirmed profile refuses before any origin or wallet read
- the wallet popover states that the wallet broadcasts through its own RPC,
  lists the profile's RPCs and offers the HTTPS ones via EIP-3085 on click

Profile changes (either mode): a tab whose saved profile changed in another
tab refuses every chain read (baseRpc, quorum readers, custody, receipts) and
every transaction (assertPlatformTransactionCurrent) until it reloads; sign-out
keeps its key. A session opened under a profile (no relay) is not served by a
hosted page through its stored RPC; independent records store no RPC.

Hosted mode is unchanged (wallet-first reads, the public default pool).
Admin migrator: no estimate request without a selected RPC.

Tests: site-browser-rpc-closure (real modules per profile state, e820e2405
control: 8/8 checks fail there), site-browser-rpc-routes (Chromium rig).
site-independent-management-unit reset keeps the saved profile.
