+  replaces or removes the saved profile, this tab refuses every chain read and every
+  transaction until it reloads. That includes custody reads and sign-out, which keeps
+  the session key. A hosted tab behaves the same when a profile is saved elsewhere. A
+  session opened under a profile (no relay) is not served by a hosted page: it would
+  read through the RPC stored with it.
+- **Custody.** Custody reads use every RPC in the profile, with its quorum,
+  confirmations and block-age limit.
